---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Affiliate Disclosure | CookMushroom" description="CookMushroom may earn a commission when you buy through Amazon links on the site. How affiliate links work here and how products are chosen.">
  <main id="content" class="guide">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective October 1, 2026</p>
    <article class="prose">
      <p><strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong></p>
      <p>CookMushroom is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</p>
      <section>
        <h2>What that means for you</h2>
        <p>Some pages may link to kitchen equipment on Amazon — pans, air fryers, mushroom brushes, knives and similar tools. If you click one of those links and buy something, CookMushroom may receive a small commission. You pay the same price either way.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>How products are chosen</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A product is mentioned because it suits the cooking method on that page, not because of its commission rate.</li>
          <li>No brand pays to be included, and commissions do not change the cooking guidance, cook times or recipes.</li>
          <li>Every guide and recipe works with ordinary equipment. You never need to buy anything to follow one.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>How affiliate links are marked</h2>
        <p>Pages that contain affiliate links carry a short notice near the top, before the first link. Prices and availability are set by Amazon and can change after a page is published.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>When you follow an affiliate link, Amazon may set cookies on your device to credit the referral. That data is handled under Amazon’s own privacy notice. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what this site itself collects.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@cookmushroom.com">hello@cookmushroom.com</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
